        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/sonic-the-hedgehog-2",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 12089,
        "name": "Fantastic Dizzy",
        "summary": "Dizzy is an egg living in a world of magic and fantasy. The basic concept of the game is to move around the world, finding various items and collectibles, and to use them in the right locations. Dizzy has no special skills or abilities, save for his remarkable feats of somersaulting, and must solve all problems he faces with the clever use of one or more items.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2b68.jpg",
        "release_date": 748569600,
        "rating": 85.94317331509087,
        "rating_count": 19,
        "genres": "Platform|Adventure|Arcade",
        "platform_ids": "29,35,13,16,18,64",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/fantastic-dizzy",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 3197,
        "name": "Shining Force II",
        "summary": "As a student of Astral the wizard, you and your friends study all the usual subjects: reading, writing, and sword fighting. As your time at school draws to an end, dark events are taking place on the island of Grans. The two Jewels which seal the Door to Darkness have been stolen, allowing a creature of awesome power to be unleashed. Finding where the Jewels were taken, and why, is a task only the bravest of adventurers can undertake.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co97f0.jpg",
        "release_date": 749433600,
        "rating": 85.4173140002901,
        "rating_count": 55,
        "genres": "Role-playing (RPG)|Strategy|Turn-based strategy (TBS)",
        "platform_ids": "3,5,29,6,14",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/shining-force-ii",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 16035,
        "name": "Kid Chameleon",
        "summary": "Kid Chameleon is a 1992 platform game released for the Sega Genesis/Mega Drive. The premise of the game is that the main character, Casey, can use masks to change into different characters in order to use different abilities. It was later released in Japan as Chameleon Kid.\n\nThe game is also a part of the Sega Genesis Collection for the PlayStation 2 and PlayStation Portable. It was released for the Virtual Console in Japan on May 22, 2007; North America on May 28, 2007; and Europe on June 1, 2007. It was also released in addition to a series of other Sega games, including Shining Force and Comix Zone, in Sega Smash Pack 2. The game has also appeared in Sonic's Ultimate Genesis Collection for Xbox 360 and PlayStation 3.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co6q7b.jpg",
        "release_date": 707011200,
        "rating": 85.01482977291003,
        "rating_count": 37,
        "genres": "Platform",
        "platform_ids": "3,5,29,34,6,39,14",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/kid-chameleon",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 8775,
        "name": "Micro Machines 2: Turbo Tournament",
        "summary": "Micro Machines 2: Turbo Tournament featured cars that require different handling techniques for each course and also hovercraft and helicopters. There are different playing modes including \"head-to-head\", in which each player earns points by driving a full screen ahead of the opponent. TV presenter Violet Berlin features as a playable driver. The MS-DOS version featured a track editor.\nA selling point for the Sega Genesis/Mega Drive version was the J-Cart, a cartridge including two control ports, thus eliminating the need for a 4-player adaptor. It also included a 'pad-sharing' feature which allowed 2 players to share a single joypad; thus it enabled 8 players to compete simultaneously, on certain tracks.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co4moc.jpg",
        "release_date": 783648000,
        "rating": 84.38726812447841,
        "rating_count": 35,
        "genres": "Racing",
        "platform_ids": "19,29,13",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/micro-machines-2-turbo-tournament",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 5164,
        "name": "Turrican",
        "summary": "Turrican is a 1990 video game programmed and designed by Manfred Trenz. It was first developed for the Commodore 64 by Rainbow Arts, but was ported to other systems later. In addition to concept design and character creation, Trenz personally programmed Turrican on the Commodore 64. A sequel, Turrican II, followed 1991 for the Commodore 64 and other platforms.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2l0v.jpg",
        "release_date": 662601600,
        "rating": 84.36908702005523,
        "rating_count": 28,
        "genres": "Shooter|Platform",
        "platform_ids": "73,15,26,29,63,86,158,16,25",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/turrican",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 4519,
        "name": "Jurassic Park",
        "summary": "Jurassic Park is a SEGA Genesis/Mega Drive game based on the first movie.\nThe game was playable as either Dr. Alan Grant or a Velociraptor (presumably the The Big One). Grant is the default character but can be changed using the 'Player' option on the game's main menu to swich to the raptor.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co2zdt.jpg",
        "release_date": 746323200,
        "rating": 83.61262025181117,
        "rating_count": 50,
        "genres": "Shooter|Platform",
        "platform_ids": "29",
        "external_url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/jurassic-park",
        "cached_at": 1772208554
      },
      {
        "id": 1653,
        "name": "Streets of Rage 2",
        "summary": "Mr. X and the Syndicate are back, this time taking Adam hostage! Take on the role of Axel, Blaze, Skate, or Max to rescue Adam, and destroy Mr. X once and for all.",
        "cover_url": "https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_big/co49sn.jpg",
        "release_date": 723168000,
